message: "If you use or reference this project, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "BrittleBench: A Defender's Audit of Public Detection Content Robustness"
abstract: >
  A large-scale empirical study measuring how robust publicly-published detection
  rules (Sigma, YARA, Elastic, Splunk) are when faced with LLM-generated functional
  mutations of the attacks those rules are designed to detect. Produces a benchmark
  dataset, an open-source toolkit, and a primary publication.
